From: Wisp Contributors <wisp@wisp.dev>
Date: May 20, 2026
Subject: feat: add Wisp OSC 777 CLI agent support to Warp

This patch adds Wisp as a fully-supported third-party CLI agent in Warp,
complete with OSC 777 event handling for status chips, approval banners,
and desktop notifications.

Wisp is an open-source, local-first coding agent powered by Ollama.
When users run `wisp --warp-mode` in Warp's terminal, the agent toolbelt
activates with full native support — footer status, approval banners,
rich input editor, code review panel, and session sharing.

Includes: CLIAgent::Wisp, WispPluginManager, OSC 777 listener support.

